// Title: Access of Sudoers File Content
// Sigma ID: 0f79c4d2-4e1f-4683-9c36-b5469a665e06
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-06-20 | Modified: 2025-06-04
// ATT&CK: reconnaissance, T1592.004
// Description: Detects the execution of a text-based file access or inspection utilities to read the content of
//   /etc/sudoers in order to potentially list all users that have sudo rights.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administration activities
// References:
//   - https://github.com/sleventyeleven/linuxprivchecker/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_susp_process_reading_sudoers.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "/cat" or FolderPath endswith "/ed" or FolderPath endswith "/egrep" or FolderPath endswith "/emacs" or FolderPath endswith "/fgrep" or FolderPath endswith "/grep" or FolderPath endswith "/head" or FolderPath endswith "/less" or FolderPath endswith "/more" or FolderPath endswith "/nano" or FolderPath endswith "/tail") and ProcessCommandLine contains " /etc/sudoers"
